# /etc/fstab — the mount table of a disk whose partition 2 is `/` (px67,
# tools/mkdisk --gpt --root): its first line names `/`, the root the
# kernel command line's `root=` mounted (its `rw` remounts it read-write
# when root= said `ro`), and /tmp is a tmpfs, the memory's (R-px67-1).
# /home is a directory of `/` (R-px67-3); /proc, /sys and /dev are the
# kernel's, over the disk's own directories. The playground's, and
# the root and journal suites' archives'. px68: `/` is ext3, journalled
# (tools/mkdisk --root's default); a `/` line's type is not acted on,
# the volume's superblock says what it is (an ext2 root, --no-journal,
# mounts the same).
/dev/vda2	/	ext3	rw	0	1
tmpfs	/tmp	tmpfs	nosuid,nodev	0	0
